# D46 rider — the `Vector[T]` cell of the element-comparability gate. Same rule
# as `Option[T]`, different container: the container is non-declarable so its
# equality is intrinsic, and the gate is on the ELEMENT. `Point` has no
# `Equatable`, so this is refused and `Point` is blamed.
#
# The container axis is covered rather than sampled: `Option` (prelude enum),
# `Vector` (prelude struct) and the anonymous tuple each get a cell, because the
# three reach the predicate through DIFFERENT `ResolvedType` variants
# (`Generic`, `Generic`, `Tuple`) and a bug can live in one arm alone.

struct Point:
    int x
    int y

void main():
    Vector[Point] a = [Point(1, 2)]
    Vector[Point] b = [Point(1, 2)]
    print(a == b)
